s for IPv4 on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline showed net.ipv4.conf.all/default.accept_redirects=1 (cmd-d52e6dbc69b74632). Executor created /etc/sysctl.d/60-icmp-redirect-hardening.conf setting all/default.accept_redirects=0, applied live with sysctl --system, and verified runtime values=0 (cmd-9d7fccb516f043f2, cmd-561590c542b845cd, cmd-31b4b78d66d549e5). Per-interface (enp1s0/lo) values remained 1 but the kernel applies AND-logic between 'all' and per-interface settings for accept_redirects, so setting 'all'=0 disables acceptance network-wide regardless of legacy per-interface values. Post-reboot verification (cmd-f662c235abf94fc5) confirms values remain 0 and the config file persisted, demonstrating true persistence across a reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d52e6dbc69b74632\",\"cmd-9d7fccb516f043f2\",\"cmd-561590c542b845cd\",\"cmd-31b4b78d66d549e5\",\"cmd-f662c235abf94fc5\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Persistently disable acceptance of source-routed packets for IPv4 on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline showed net.ipv4.conf.default.accept_source_route=1 (net.ipv4.conf.all.accept_source_route was already 0) (cmd-d52e6dbc69b74632). Executor's new config file sets all/default.accept_source_route=0, applied and verified live (cmd-9d7fccb516f043f2, cmd-561590c542b845cd, cmd-31b4b78d66d549e5). Same AND-logic applies for accept_source_route, so the 'all'=0 setting is effective network-wide despite per-interface residual value=1. Post-reboot verification (cmd-f662c235abf94fc5) confirms values remain 0 and config persisted.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d52e6dbc69b74632\",\"cmd-9d7fccb516f043f2\",\"cmd-561590c542b845cd\",\"cmd-31b4b78d66d549e5\",\"cmd-f662c235abf94fc5\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Configuration takes effect without conflicting with existing persistent sysctl settings\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Executor inspected existing /etc/sysctl.d/*.conf files and /etc/sysctl.conf before creating the new file, confirming any existing directives for these settings were commented out or unrelated (rp_filter only), so the new 60-icmp-redirect-hardening.conf file applies cleanly without conflict.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c13168c161b14efc\",\"cmd-732ec3fe3d3e4481\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Mandatory provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline boot_id=37344ae4... captured (cmd-b805256b29794c4f), matching the global before_prepare boot-identity snapshot. Restart acknowledged via backgrounded reboot command returning before disconnect (cmd-e3e322077ba440e8). Node observed unreachable mid-reboot (cmd-0d65495a79d343f5). Post-restart boot_id=d5be2f6d... differs from baseline (cmd-0625063076124e10), matching the global after_executor boot-identity snapshot. Recovered state confirmed: sysctl values and config file intact post-reboot (cmd-f662c235abf94fc5), and global after_executor snapshot shows no failed services and healthy package state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b805256b29794c4f\",\"cmd-e3e322077ba440e8\",\"cmd-0d65495a79d343f5\",\"cmd-0625063076124e10\",\"cmd-f662c235abf94fc5\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.97,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands trace to a clear purpose: baseline discovery (read-only), config file creation (cmd-9d7fccb516f043f2), live application via sysctl --system (cmd-561590c542b845cd), and the mandated restart protocol (cmd-e3e322077ba440e8) which was bounded, cleanly executed, and fully verified afterward. No unnecessary mutations, abandoned files, or conflicting services were found; the after_executor snapshot shows no failed services, unchanged package-health status, and only expected systemd-private tmp directories tied to the new boot session (not executor residue).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9d7fccb516f043f2\",\"cmd-561590c542b845cd\",\"cmd-e3e322077ba440e8\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor persistently disabled IPv4 ICMP-redirect and source-routed-packet acceptance on node1 by creating /etc/sysctl.d/60-icmp-redirect-hardening.conf, applying it live, and verifying the change survived a full reboot with a changed boot identity, matching the fixed global boot-identity snapshots. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was also satisfied with a clean pre/post transition and no residual issues.\",\"limitations\":[\"Per-interface (enp1s0/lo) accept_redirects and accept_source_route values remained at 1 after the change; the assessment relies on documented Linux kernel AND-logic between 'all' and per-interface settings for these two parameters to conclude the change is effective network-wide, since a live packet-level test of redirect/source-route rejection was not captured.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of ICMP redirects for IPv4 on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline showed net.ipv4.conf.all/default.accept_redirects=1 (cmd-d52e6dbc69b74632). Executor created /etc/sysctl.d/60-icmp-redirect-hardening.conf setting all/default.accept_redirects=0, applied live with sysctl --system, and verified runtime values=0 (cmd-9d7fccb516f043f2, cmd-561590c542b845cd, cmd-31b4b78d66d549e5). Per-interface (enp1s0/lo) values remained 1 but the kernel applies AND-logic between 'all' and per-interface settings for accept_redirects, so setting 'all'=0 disables acceptance network-wide regardless of legacy per-interface values. Post-reboot verification (cmd-f662c235abf94fc5) confirms values remain 0 and the config file persisted, demonstrating true persistence across a reboot.","ev